INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(400, 0, 4, 0, 0, 0, 'Blasted Lands', 'The Blasted Lands were once the southern half of the Black Morass, a dark fen of marsh and mire. It was here that Medivh and the warlocks of the Shadow Council opened the Dark Portal, and the orcish Horde poured through into Azeroth. The energies of the gate dried and warped the land into a red and barren waste where lightning flickers without end and even the beasts have grown unnaturally strong. At the close of the Second War the broken Horde made its last stand at the foot of the portal, and afterwards the Kirin Tor raised Nethergarde Keep in the northern hills to keep watch. Twenty years of silence ended when demons burst through the gate, and now the armies of the Alliance and the Horde march through the wastes and on into Outland. Yet the demons never truly left. The dreadlord Razelikh rules the wastes through his Shadowsworn cult and the Dreadmaul ogres, and the Burning Legion''s soldiers still gather in the Tainted Scar.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Blasted_Lands (southern part of the Black Morass, dried and warped by the portal''s magic, constant lightning, Nethergarde built by Khadgar and the Kirin Tor, Razelikh and the Shadowsworn, Legion in the Tainted Scar); gameobject 175745 The Dark Portal and the Fall of Stormwind (Medivh and the Shadow Council opened the portal); gameobject 21581 Aftermath of the Second War (last battle at the foot of the portal); npc_text 1351 (beasts changed by the portal''s energy); npc_text 8770 (demons surged from the portal); quest 10119 description (20 years silent)'),
(401, 1, 4, 1, 0, 0, 'Nethergarde Keep', 'Nethergarde Keep stands in the northern hills of the Blasted Lands, a Dalaranian fortress raised after the Second War at the urging of Archmage Khadgar to guard against any new invasion through the Dark Portal. The Kirin Tor have manned it ever since, and its analysts and riftwatchers keep a close eye on the gate. Khadgar himself held command here until the gate was reopened and he led the Alliance into Draenor. Today the keep lives on supplies sent from Darkshire, too many of which go astray on the road, its library holds histories of the portal''s wars, and an ambassador within its walls urges the Alliance to set aside its quarrel with the Horde and face the true enemy.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Nethergarde_Keep (Dalaranian fortress built after the Second War at Khadgar''s behest to prevent further invasions from Draenor, staffed by the Kirin Tor, Khadgar led it until the portal reopened, mage tower); gameobject 21582 Beyond the Dark Portal (portal reopened a few months after Nethergarde''s completion); gameobjects 21581, 21582, 175745 (history books in the keep); DB spawns in area 1438: Nethergarde Analyst 6001, Nethergarde Riftwatcher 6002, Ambassador Ardalan 7826; quests 1395, 1423, 1425 (supplies from Darkshire, lost supplies); quest 2783 description (we fight the wrong enemy); quest 1423 reward text (so many supplies are lost between Darkshire and the keep)'),
(402, 1, 4, 2, 0, 0, 'Garrison Armory', 'In the hills beside Nethergarde Keep, the Garrison Armory is the keep''s working mine. Nethergarde miners, watched over by foremen and engineers, cut mithril and truesilver from the rock, and what they dig is sent to Stormwind in trade for the many supplies a fortress in the wastes cannot produce for itself. Its tunnels run deep beneath the hills. The crews guard their ore jealously, and any Horde prospector who slips inside hoping to work the veins will find the miners turning on him at once.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Garrison_Armory (Alliance mining outpost, miners gather resources for the keep, traded to Stormwind; Horde could mine there but the NPCs attack them); DB spawns: Nethergarde Miner 5996, Foreman 5998, Engineer 5997 in area 1457 and in underground tunnels (negative z) under the hills toward the swamp; Mithril Deposit 150079 and Truesilver Deposit 150081 in area 1457; factiontemplate 1575 (Nethergarde miners hostile to Horde)'),
(403, 1, 4, 3, 0, 0, 'Dreadmaul Hold', 'In the northwest corner of the Blasted Lands squats Dreadmaul Hold, once an orc settlement until the Dreadmaul ogres drove the orcs out after the Second War and gave it their own name. Behind its barracks and smithy, ogres, ogre mages and brutes answer to Grol the Destroyer, who serves Razelikh the Defiler in return for a life without end. Near his seat stand stones of binding, each holding souls of the Horde soldiers whom the Defiler handed to Grol as servants. Starving snickerfang hyenas lurk at the edges of the camp, and a rarely seen ogre called Mojo the Twisted walks among the brutes.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dreadmaul_Hold (northwest corner, ogres forced out the orcs after the Second War and renamed it, barracks and blacksmith, Grol serves Razelikh); quests 2681, 2744 (Servants of Grol, triad granted unending life in the Blasted Lands); DB spawns in area 1437: Dreadmaul Ogre 5974, Ogre Mage 5975, Brute 5976, Grol the Destroyer 7665, Servant of Grol 7669, Stone of Binding 141857, Starving Snickerfang 5984, Mojo the Twisted 8296 (rare)'),
(404, 1, 4, 4, 0, 0, 'Altar of Storms', 'On the western edge of the wastes stands the Altar of Storms, one of the few such altars left in Azeroth, raised here by Lady Sevine, one of the three masters of the Shadowsworn. Her followers keep it: enforcers, warlocks and dreadweavers who have given themselves over to the demon lord Razelikh. Sevine holds court beside the altar, and a stone of binding nearby imprisons souls of the Horde regiment Thrall''s Grasp, torn from their bodies by the Defiler and given to her as servants.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Altar_of_Storms_(Blasted_Lands) (western edge, built by Lady Sevine); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shadowsworn (controlled by the Shadowsworn, one of the remaining altars in Azeroth); DB spawns in area 1441: Shadowsworn Enforcer 6007, Warlock 6008, Dreadweaver 6009, Lady Sevine 7667, Servant of Sevine 7671, Stone of Binding 141859; quest 2681 objectives (Servants of Sevine)'),
(405, 1, 4, 5, 0, 0, 'Rise of the Defiler', 'The craggy peaks at the heart of the Blasted Lands belong to Razelikh the Defiler. His lair sits on the highest summit, reachable only by runes of teleportation, and a spirit called the Deathly Usher, bound eternally to this cursed world, waits below to send up any who would face him. There, at the Altar of the Defiler, the demon lord can be called forth by one who carries his amulet. Nearby, in a crater, lives Kum''isha the Collector, one of the Lost Ones, who gathers draenethyst in the hope of opening a road back to the world he lost.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Rise_of_the_Defiler (craggy mountains near the middle, home of Razelikh); quest 3628 description (lair atop the highest mountain, teleport runes, use the amulet on the Altar of the Defiler); npc_text 2213 and gossip option ''I wish to face the Defiler.'' (Deathly Usher 8816); DB spawns in area 2517: Deathly Usher 8816, Altar of the Defiler 153205, Kum''isha 7363; creature_text 7363 (why I live in a crater); quest 2521 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kum%27isha_the_Collector (Lost One)'),
(406, 1, 4, 6, 0, 0, 'The Serpent''s Coil', 'The Serpent''s Coil is a winding cave system in the eastern Blasted Lands, its mouth ringed by the burnt-out shells of orcish buildings left from the Second War. Shadowsworn cultists, thugs and adepts guard it for Archmage Allistarj, the master of this labyrinth. In these halls Allistarj tortured the captured commander of Thrall''s Grasp and his lieutenant Kirith, and the screams of his experiments rang through the caves. Kirith never left. What he became still prowls the back cave, and a stone of binding nearby holds more souls of the fallen regiment. Redstone basilisks hunt among the ruins.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Serpent%27s_Coil (winding cave system in eastern Blasted Lands, burnt-out orcish structures from the Second War, Allistarj operated his Shadowsworn from within); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fallen_Hero_of_the_Horde (Kirith roams the back cave of the Serpent''s Coil); quest 2721 description (tortured by Allistarj, screams through the halls of the cave); DB spawns in area 1440: Shadowsworn Cultist 6004, Thug 6005, Adept 6006, Archmage Allistarj 7666, Servant of Allistarj 7670, Stone of Binding 141858, Redstone Basilisk 5990'),
(407, 1, 4, 7, 0, 0, 'Dreadmaul Post', 'Dreadmaul Post is an ogre mound of the Dreadmaul clan, raised in the wastes nearer the Dark Portal, through which the ogres first came from Draenor and close to which they have stayed ever since. Dreadmaul maulers and warlocks hold it, and felbeasts prowl the ground around it. Here too stands a stone of binding where Grol keeps souls taken from Thrall''s Grasp. Now and then a rarely seen ogre known as Magronos the Unyielding walks among them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dreadmaul_Post (ogre mound of the Dreadmaul clan; Dreadmaul remained close to the Dark Portal after coming from Draenor); DB spawns in area 1439: Dreadmaul Mauler 5977, Dreadmaul Warlock 5978, Felbeast 8675, Servant of Grol 7669, Stone of Binding 141857, Magronos the Unyielding 8297 (rare)'),
(408, 1, 4, 8, 0, 0, 'The Dark Portal', 'The Dark Portal looms over the southern Blasted Lands, the colossal gate through which the orcish Horde first came to Azeroth. Shattered at the end of the Second War, it woke once more for a short while and then stood silent for twenty years, until the Burning Legion forced demons through it. Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn held them at bay until the kingdoms of Azeroth arrived and drove them back to Outland. The camps at its foot are calm now, and Alliance and Horde commanders send every soldier they can up the steps and through the gate. Felguard sentries and felhounds still roam the approaches, and stones of binding there hold souls of Thrall''s Grasp.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dark_Portal (Horde came through it, destroyed after the Second War, silent about twenty years, Kazzak''s ritual reopened it, Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn with Alliance and Horde pushed the demons back); npc_text 8770 (Relthorn: battle, Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn, camp now calm); npc_text 9969 (Dar''toon); quests 10119, 9407; DB spawns in area 72: Felguard Sentry 6011, Felhound 6010, Servant of Razelikh 7668, Stone of Binding 141812, Relthorn 16841, Dar''toon 19254; gameobject 21582 Beyond the Dark Portal (portal woke again months after Nethergarde was finished, later destroyed from Draenor)'),
(409, 1, 4, 9, 0, 0, 'The Tainted Scar', 'In the southwest of the Blasted Lands lies the Tainted Scar, where the portal''s energies left the soil the color of blood. It is the Burning Legion''s stronghold on this side of the gate, where felguard elites, manahounds, dreadlords and doomguard commanders gather in strength. After the Legion''s defeat at Mount Hyjal, Lord Kazzak led its remnants here, and from the Scar he sent Razelikh to bring the wastes to heel. When the Dark Portal opened once more, Kazzak passed through into Outland. At an altar on the northern edge the aged warlock Daio the Decrepit lives among the demons, teaching others to bind them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tainted_Scar (barren soil the color of blood; Kazzak in the Scar until the portal reopened, then entered Outland; Daio settled at its altar); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Blasted_Lands (after Hyjal Kazzak led the remaining Legion forces in the Tainted Scar and sent Razelikh to secure the land); DB spawns in area 73: Felguard Elite 8717, Manahound 8718, Doomguard Commander 12396, Dreadlord 8716, Daio the Decrepit 14463; quests 7581-7583'),
(410, 2, 4, 1, 0, 0, 'Razelikh the Defiler', 'Razelikh the Defiler is a dreadlord whose true name is Rakh''likh, once the most feared of Lord Kazzak''s lieutenants. Sent to secure the Blasted Lands after the Legion''s retreat, he forged the Shadowsworn from scattered sects of the Shadow Council and the Dreadmaul ogres, and granted his three chief servants near-limitless power in exchange for eternal service. It was Razelikh who tore the souls from the soldiers of Thrall''s Grasp and bound them to stones. He keeps to the heights of the Rise of the Defiler and appears only when summoned at his altar with his own amulet, calling Ilifar, Keeper of Souls, to fight at his side.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Razelikh_the_Defiler (dreadlord, true name Rakh''likh, Kazzak''s most fearsome lieutenant, tasked with securing the land, united the Shadow Council); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shadowsworn (formed by uniting Shadow Council sects with the Dreadmaul); quests 2681, 2744, 3628 (descriptions); creature_text 7664 (Ilifar, your master calls; Face my champion); creature_template 7734 Ilifar <Keeper of Souls>'),
(411, 2, 4, 2, 0, 0, 'Allistarj, Sevine and Grol', 'Three servants rule the Blasted Lands in Razelikh''s name: Archmage Allistarj of the Serpent''s Coil, Lady Sevine, who raised the Altar of Storms, and Grol the Destroyer, master of the Dreadmaul ogres. Each pledged eternal service to the dreadlord and received in return a third of an amulet of his making, the very key needed to summon him. The pieces are bound to their owners'' lifeforce, so that within the Blasted Lands none of the three can be slain by ordinary means. Each was also given souls of Thrall''s Grasp as servants, and it was Allistarj who tortured the regiment''s captured commander and his lieutenant Kirith.', 'quest 2743 description (each underling wears a third of the amulet); quest 2744 description (immortal within the Blasted Lands, nearly unlimited power); quest 2681 objectives; quest 2721 description (tortured by Allistarj); quest 3627 objectives; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shadowsworn; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Altar_of_Storms_(Blasted_Lands); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dreadmaul_Hold'),
(412, 2, 4, 3, 0, 0, 'Kirith', 'Kirith was lieutenant to the commander of Thrall''s Grasp, and was taken alive with him when the regiment was overwhelmed in the Blasted Lands. Both were handed over to Archmage Allistarj, but where his commander endured, Kirith''s will faltered, and his screams rang through the halls of the cave as the experiments went on. What came out was Kirith the Damned, a great fel beast that roams the back cave of the Serpent''s Coil. Only death can free what remains of him. His spirit lingers for a short while afterward, grinning and blunt, long enough to tell how the Defiler''s servants guard the secret of summoning their master.', 'quest 2721 description and reward text; quest 2743 description (Kirith grins, my time here is limited); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kirith (Horde lieutenant, tortured by Allistarj, soul twisted into a beast, found in the Serpent''s Coil cave; defeating him draws out his spirit); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fallen_Hero_of_the_Horde (Kirith roams the back cave as a huge felhunter)'),
(413, 2, 4, 4, 0, 0, 'Kum''isha the Collector', 'Kum''isha the Collector is one of the Lost Ones, a draenei exile who lives in a crater near the Rise of the Defiler, stranded far from his homeland. He has given his life to the search for flawless spheres of draenethyst, crystals so rare that draenei have died seeking a single one, for with them he believes he can open a rift back to the world he lost. To his senses every race of Azeroth gives off the same dizzying reek of greed, and since it was greed that cost him his home, he means to let greed carry him back. He pays in trinkets for any fragment brought to him, and despises those who take the payment.', 'npc_text 1302, 1303; quests 2521, 2522, 3501, 3502 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 7363; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kum%27isha_the_Collector; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kum%27isha_the_Collector (race Lost One; pre-Cataclysm he opens a portal and goes through with other Lost Ones)'),
(414, 2, 4, 5, 0, 0, 'Bloodmages Drazial and Lynnore', 'Bloodmage Drazial and his sister Lynnore, elven practitioners of blood magic, keep a small camp near the northern entrance to the Blasted Lands. They believe the energy unleashed when the Dark Portal opened seeped into the beasts of the region and drove them to evolve into their present forms. Drazial studies the body: hyena jowls able to snap through thorium steel, the lungs of blasted boars, the decisive strike of the scorpok. Lynnore studies mind and spirit, from the cunning of the redstone basilisk to the vigor hidden in vulture gizzards. Both distill their findings into potent assays, though Drazial''s love of science never strays far from thoughts of profit.', 'npc_text 1351, 1371; quests 2581-2586 and 2601-2604 (descriptions); quest 2585 description (wealthy beyond our... I mean...); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Bloodmage_Drazial (blood elf, sister Lynnore, stationed near the entrance to the Blasted Lands); DB spawns 7505 and 7506 at -10884,-2935 (map 50,14), faction 35'),
(415, 2, 4, 6, 1, 0, 'Quartermaster Lungertz', 'Quartermaster Lungertz keeps Nethergarde Keep supplied, no easy task at the far end of a road that winds through Deadwind Pass and the Swamp of Sorrows. Crates of powerstones for the keep''s mages must be rushed from Darkshire before their power fades, barrels stamped with his name turn up lost along the way, and when Watcher Biggs'' caravan was ambushed in the swamp he gave it up for gone. And he waits on Azoran crystals, a reagent the keep''s wizards are running short of. As he reminds every visitor, Nethergarde always needs more: supplies for its mages'' research and supplies to keep its defenders fit to fight.', 'quest 1395 description and texts; quest 1423 description and reward text; quest 1425 reward text (Azoran Crystals, Biggs'' caravan thought lost); quest_greeting 5393 (Nethergarde always needs more supplies, for the mages'' research and the defenders)'),
(416, 2, 4, 7, 1, 0, 'Watcher Mahar Ba', 'Watcher Mahar Ba is one of the watchers of Nethergarde Keep, a scholar eager to understand the forces at work around him. For a long while he waited on a request sent to Master Mazen of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences in Stormwind: Khadgar''s Essays on Dimensional Convergence, the writings of the very archmage at whose urging the keep was built. The young courier carrying them lost his way in the Swamp of Sorrows and dropped the essays as he fled from plantlike creatures of the marsh, and only a determined traveler brought them on. The chance to glimpse the insight of one as great as Khadgar excites him beyond words.', 'quest 1364 description and reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Nethergarde_Keep (built at Khadgar''s behest); DB spawn 5385 in Nethergarde Keep, faction template 53 (hostile to Horde)'),
(417, 2, 4, 8, 1, 0, 'Thadius Grimshade', 'Thadius Grimshade is a Wildhammer dwarf who left Aerie Peak years ago in pursuit of darker knowledge, and now works as a diviner in the mage tower of Nethergarde Keep. His rituals can follow the thread between an object and its owner, though he warns onlookers to make no sound, since a single misstep could spell their doom. He does nothing for free. When the gryphon master of Aerie Peak sought his help to find the lost gryphon Sharpbeak, Grimshade first demanded the medallion of the Zul''Farrak troll Nekrum, hoping to learn how it had lengthened its bearer''s life without paying its unpleasant price.', 'quests 2990, 2991, 2992, 2993 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 8022; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thadius_Grimshade'),
(418, 2, 4, 9, 0, 0, 'Daio the Decrepit', 'Daio the Decrepit is an aged human warlock, once a mage, who has settled at an altar on the northern edge of the Tainted Scar among the Legion''s own soldiers. There he teaches the infernal arts to younger warlocks, above all the binding of greater demons. To cage a doomguard, he teaches, one needs a crystal prison shaped from the Tears of the Hederine, an anti-magic crystal from the demons of Winterspring, bound with the blood of the Wildspawn satyrs of Dire Maul, and even then the demon will fight savagely against capture. He holds no illusions about such power: those who wield it, he says, pay grossly for it.', 'quests 7581, 7582, 7583 (descriptions and reward texts); npc_text 6995; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Daio_the_Decrepit (elderly human warlock, formerly a mage, altar in the northern Tainted Scar, trains recruits, ''we pay grossly for the use of said powers''); broadcast_text 9611 (we pay grossly for the use of said powers)'),
(419, 2, 4, 10, 0, 0, 'Netherwane and Dar''toon', 'At the foot of the Dark Portal two camps stand side by side. Watch Commander Relthorn Netherwane of Nethergarde remembers the battle fought here not long ago, when the keep and the Argent Dawn held back a tide of demons until the kingdoms of Azeroth came to drive them through the gate. He never thought to see the portal open again, and fears the quiet hides the madness beyond it. Warlord Dar''toon of the Horde speaks of the same battle with open envy, wishing he had been there when the demons clashed with Azeroth''s heroes. Both now send every soldier they can spare through the gate to the war in Outland.', 'npc_text 8770 (Relthorn); npc_text 9969 (Dar''toon); quest 10119 description (I never thought to see this day); quest 9407 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Watch_Commander_Relthorn_Netherwane (Nethergarde)'),
(420, 3, 4, 1, 0, 0, 'Through the Dark Portal', 'For twenty years the Dark Portal stood silent, a monument to wars half forgotten. The histories kept at Nethergarde tell its story. Opened by Medivh and the Shadow Council, it carried the Horde into Azeroth, and when the Horde broke at the end of the Second War its last clans fell at the foot of the gate. A few months after the keep was finished the portal woke again, and Khadgar and Turalyon led the Alliance into Draenor, then destroyed the gate from the far side to spare Azeroth, their own fate unknown. Then the Burning Legion forced it open once more. Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn held until the armies of the Alliance and the Horde drove the demons back. Now both sides call for volunteers to cross, for beyond the gate rages a savage war that their commanders fear cannot be won without fresh strength from Azeroth.', 'quests 10119, 9407 (descriptions and reward texts); gameobjects 21581, 21582, 175745 (Nethergarde books); npc_text 8770; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dark_Portal (Stair of Destiny is the Outland counterpart in Hellfire Peninsula); quest_template 10288, 10120 (follow-ups start at the Outland end, so 10119 and 9407 are the Blasted Lands entry quests)'),
(421, 3, 4, 2, 0, 0, 'The Fall of the Defiler', 'Once the souls of Thrall''s Grasp were freed from their stones, the regiment''s fallen commander turned to the one man still missing: his lieutenant Kirith, last heard screaming under Archmage Allistarj''s experiments. Kirith was found in the Serpent''s Coil, twisted into a fel beast, and only in death could his spirit speak. He revealed that Allistarj, Lady Sevine and Grol each wear a third of Razelikh''s amulet, the key to summoning the Defiler, and that the pieces make them deathless within the Blasted Lands. The search for a weapon led to the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes in Azshara, to azsharite crystals from the south of that land, and to Galvan the Ancient of the Mithril Order in Stranglethorn, who forged fel weapons able to weaken the three. Armed at last, the hero''s champions slew the triad, joined the amulet and bore it to the altar atop the Rise of the Defiler. Razelikh fell, and his severed horn was carried back as proof that heroes still exist.', 'quests 2721, 2743, 2744, 3141, 3602, 3621, 3625, 3626, 3627, 3628 (descriptions and reward texts); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Razelikh_the_Defiler; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fallen_Hero_of_the_Horde'),
(422, 3, 4, 3, 0, 0, 'Kum''isha''s Spheres', 'Somewhere in the Blasted Lands, Kum''isha the Collector insists, flawless spheres of draenethyst can still be found, though draenei have spent whole lifetimes searching for one and died with their purpose unfulfilled. Any creature of the wastes might carry one. He asks anyone willing, greedy as he believes them all to be, to bring him such a sphere in exchange for riches. When one at last reaches him he can hardly believe it. He sets it hovering before him, chants in an unknown tongue and tears open a rift, crying out to his brethren to rise and go home to Outland before it closes. Yet afterward he counts the conjuration a failure and waits for another sphere. Meanwhile he buys flawed fragments, which may still serve his people in other ways, paying in trinkets and scorn alike. His junk heap shrinks while theirs grows, which on Draenor, he says, counts as a fair trade.', 'quests 2521, 2522, 3501, 3502 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 7363 groups 0-4; npc_text 1302');
